    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll** (75.70) and **Seiya Suzuki** (71.14), our premier offensive threats. **Corbin Carroll** faces Kevin Gausman, but the matchup is deceptively favorable due to Gausman\u2019s slower delivery, which provides a significant boost for stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical priority given our league\u2019s scarcity weighting. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.27 xERA), slotting into the #2 hole where he should see high-leverage counting stat opportunities. **Henry Bolte** also earns a \"Strong\" start (61.01) by virtue of his leadoff status against Zebby Matthews, where his combination of park adjustment and order-driven volume outweighs the minor platoon penalty.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Griffin Conine**, whose raw talent and xwOBA remain high, but he ultimately landed at 35.44 due to a brutal combination of a tough matchup against Ranger Suarez and an unfavorable batting order position (#8). While **Griffin Conine** offers power, the lack of projected stolen base equity keeps him on the pine in favor of the higher-floor volume provided by **Mickey Moniak** (57.78), who benefits from a massive platoon advantage (+14%) against Cade Cavalli. We are navigating significant risk today with \"Lineup Pending\" statuses across the board, particularly with **Gabriel Moreno**, whose #3 spot is vital to his 56.63 score; should he drop down the order, his utility diminishes rapidly. **Zach McKinstry** remains a fragile play (40.98), barely clinging to a starting spot; while the wind blowing out provides a marginal buffer, he is the most likely candidate to be swapped if official lineups suggest a defensive substitution or rest day for any of our core depth pieces like **James Wood** or **Brice Turang**.",
